.TH UIGO 2
.SH NAME
uigo \- ui(4) from Go
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
import "ui"

func New(title string) (*Ui, error)
func Open(srv string) (*Ui, error)
func NewUi(rw io.ReadWriteCloser) (*Ui, error)
func (u *Ui) Ctl(format string, a ...any) error
func (u *Ui) Set(id, key, value string) error
func (u *Ui) Event() (Event, error)
func (u *Ui) ReadFile(name string) ([]byte, error)
func (u *Ui) Close() error
func Quote(v string) string

type Event struct { Kind, ID, Arg string }
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Package
.B ui
is a client of
.IR ui (4)
in Go, without cgo, as
.IR ui (2)
is in C.
.I New
starts
.B /bin/ui
in a new window
.RB ( window
in
.IR rio (1));
.I Open
takes one posted as
.BI /srv/ srv\fR.
Either mounts the
.B /srv
file on
.BI /mnt/ srv
(a directory of mntgen's, nobody else's) and uses the files there: the
kernel's 9P, whose session others share when they mount the same.
.I NewUi
speaks 9P itself, over a connection of the program's own that has no
kernel's mount behind it: a network one to
.IR exportfs (4),
or from another system.
.PP
.I Ctl
writes one transaction,
.I Set
one property
.RI ( Quote
quotes as
.IR rc (1)
does, where a value needs it),
.I Event
waits for the next line of
.B event
(an error when
.I ui
is gone),
.I ReadFile
reads any of
.IR ui 's
files
.RB ( tree ,
.BI nodes/ id /props\fR,
\&...).
.SH EXAMPLES
A window's files given to the network, and a counter in it from there
.RB ( gocount ,
in the source):
.IP
.EX
aux/listen1 -t tcp!*!5640 exportfs -r /mnt/ui &
gocount -d tcp!host!5640
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/libui/go
(module
.BR ui ;
built with ../9front-go's toolchain)
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ui (4),
.IR ui (2),
.IR uiview (2)
.SH BUGS
A
.B /srv
file must not be given to
.IR NewUi :
a second 9P session on it ends the kernel's.
